Houston</publisher-loc><publisher-name>The University of Texas M.D. Anderson Cancer Center</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b12-cin-03-219"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coombes</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsavachidis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Baggerly</surname><given-names>KA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>M-C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuerer</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Improved peak detection and quantification of mass spectrometry data acquired from surface-enhanced laser desorption and ionization by denoising spectra with the undecimated discrete wavelet transform</article-title><source>Proteomics</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>4107</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16254928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-cin-03-219"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Waele</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><source>Automatic Inference from finite time observations of Stationary stochastic signals</source><publisher-name>Wageningen</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Delft University of Technology</publisher-loc></citation></ref><ref id="b14-cin-03-219"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Waele</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Broersen</surname><given-names>PMT</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>The Burg algorithm for segments</article-title><source>IEEE Transactions on Signal Processing</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>2876</fpage><lpage>80</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15-cin-03-219"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-ty